<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Limes Museum Aalen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1964">1964</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Limesmuseum Aalen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Limes Museum in Aalen, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, is a museum of the Roman frontier in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, opened in 1964 on the site of the largest cavalry fort on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raetian-limes">Raetian Limes</a>. The fort housed the ala II Flavia, a cavalry regiment of about 1,000 men. The museum presents the Upper Germanic-Raetian Limes, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div>
